1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
This is Andy McDonald and I am a Scoutmaster with Troop 196 in Winnersprings, Florida.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:10,000
This edition of the Scoutmaster podcast is sponsored by backers like me.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,000
And now for you, Scoutmaster.

4
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:22,000
So I'm always after you, aren't I about stepping back?

5
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Let scouts do stuff. Let them make their own mistakes- right

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:32,000
And not dangerous mistakes- but let them experiment and explore and find things out for themselves

7
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:35,000
And then you know you can help them with it afterwards.

8
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Here's a great story about that from Bess Elwell Cook, who is a Girl Guides Leader in Australia.

9
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:51,000
She sent me this story Apparently one meeting. the guides were making something that the Australians call Anzac Biscuits

10
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:56,000
And a rough translation is oatmeal cookies. okay,

11
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:01,000
And one of the patrols ran out of sugar

12
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:09,000
And they decided that baking soda- you know that looks like sugar- that will just use baking soda instead.

13
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:17,000
That's the kind of mistake that has immediate consequences that they learn about very quickly

14
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:19,000
And they're probably not going to make that one again.

15
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Bess said that they did learn that that was probably not a great substitution to make in baking and that the faces were priceless.

16
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:30,000
I imagine they were.

17
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Hey, this is podcast number 217..

